# Food Safety Domain Constraints

## Deterministic control

- Critical failures must trigger deterministic rules configured from approved business evidence.
- AI must never make final food-safety, QA, loading-release, CAPA-closure, or access-control decisions.

## Record integrity

- Submitted and approved records must not be edited in place.
- Corrections require amendments with full before/after history.
- Preserve history instead of deleting operational records.

## Evidence

- Evidence files live in object storage; metadata and linkage live in PostgreSQL.
- Evidence access must be controlled and auditable.

## Business rules

- Temperature limits, CCP/OPRP classifications, checklist content, approval chains, and similar rules must come from named business owners with documented evidence sources.
- Until approved, treat such values as unconfirmed — do not hard-code invented figures.

## Continuity

- Factory-floor recording must remain possible when ERP is unavailable.
- Emergency paper fallback and retrospective entry rules require QA-approved procedures before operational use.
